-- title:
--   Normalisation of the x-chart commutes with base change to A
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and write $R = \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ and let $x \in F_0$ be such that $F_0$ is algebraic over the subfield $\mathbb{Q}(x)$ generated by $x$. Put $B =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg R F₀ {x}`, the subalgebra of $F_0$ of elements integral over $R[x]$. Assume that $\mathbb{Q} \otimes_R B$ is a smooth $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra and that $B/pB$ (the quotient by the ideal generated by the image of $p$) is reduced. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $K'$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(q)\!)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!) \to L(\!(q)\!)$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, carrying an $R$-algebra structure compatible with $L$ and such that the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $A$ act on $K'$ through $L$. Finally let $x' \in K'$ have coefficientwise image equal to that of $x$. The conclusion is that there is an isomorphism of $A$-algebras $e : A \otimes_R B \to$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg A K' {x'}`, the elements of $K'$ integral over $A[x']$, such that for every $b \in B$ the element $e(1 \otimes b)$, viewed in $L(\!(q)\!)$, is the coefficientwise image of $b$.
--
--   This is the statement that forming the integral closure of $R[x]$ in $F_0$ commutes with base change along $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to A$ for an arbitrary discrete valuation ring $A$ of residue characteristic $p$, under the hypotheses that the generic fibre is smooth and the special fibre is reduced; it is the non-smooth counterpart of the corresponding base-change statement for chart algebras that are smooth over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. It is used to identify the finite and infinite chart algebras of the Igusa scheme after base change to a field of characteristic zero.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_algEquiv_tensorProduct_chartAlg_laurentBaseChange_of_smooth_genericFibre_of_isReduced_specialFibre.lean

